     \text{overlap width} = \min(w_1, w_2) = \min(8, 8.5) = 8 \text{ inches}
     \]
   - The height of the overlapping region is the minimum of the two heights:
     \[
     \text{overlap height} = \min(h_1, h_2) = \min(10, 11) = 10 \text{ inches}
     \]

3. **Calculating the Area of Overlap**:
   - Now, we can calculate the area of the overlapping region:
     \[
     \text{overlap area} = \text{overlap width} \times \text{overlap height} = 8 \times 10 = 80 \text{ square inches}
     \]

