### Code Output Interpretation
The code output indicates that the \(1000^{\text{th}}\) term of the sequence is \(1036\). This means that after filtering out all perfect squares, cubes, and fifth powers from the list of positive integers, the \(1000^{\text{th}}\) valid number is \(1036\).

### Final Answer
Thus, the \(1000^{\text{th}}\) term of the sequence is:

\[
\boxed{1036}
\]
