     \[
     \text{gear1\_turns\_per\_minute} = 33 + \frac{1}{3} = \frac{100}{3} \text{ turns per minute}
     \]
     The time taken for one rotation of the first gear is:
     \[
     \text{gear1\_time\_per\_rotation} = \frac{60 \text{ seconds}}{\text{gear1\_turns\_per\_minute}} = \frac{60}{\frac{100}{3}} = \frac{60 \times 3}{100} = \frac{180}{100} = 1.8 \text{ seconds}
     \]

   - For the second gear:
     \[
     \text{gear2\_turns\_per\_minute} = 45 \text{ turns per minute}
     \]
     The time taken for one rotation of the second gear is:
     \[
     \text{gear2\_time\_per\_rotation} = \frac{60 \text{ seconds}}{\text{gear2\_turns\_per\_minute}} = \frac{60}{45} = \frac{4}{3} \text{ seconds}
     \]

2. **Convert Time per Rotation to Integer Seconds**:
   - Convert the time per rotation into integer seconds:
