   \]
   Thus, the inverse of \( 7 \) modulo \( 50 \) is \( -7 \equiv 43 \pmod{50} \).

### Step 5: Solving for \( u \)

Now we can multiply both sides of the simplified congruence by \( 43 \):

\[
u \equiv 23 \times 43 \pmod{50}.
\]

Calculating \( 23 \times 43 \):

\[
