\text{Favorable Outcomes} = 6 \text{ (from Case 1)} + 1 \text{ (from Case 2)} = 7
\]

### Probability Calculation
Now, we can calculate the probability that Team A is selected at least twice:

\[
P(\text{A selected at least twice}) = \frac{\text{Favorable Outcomes}}{\text{Total Outcomes}} = \frac{7}{27}
\]

